/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The term barrier means hurdle, hindrance or obstacle. Thus, barriers to communication imply hurdles or obstacles on the way of transmission of message from the sender to the receiver. In practice, there exist several barriers in communication which render it ineffective. They generate confusion, conflict and misunderstanding in the organization by creating bottlenecks, delays and distortions of information. )
/E (The term barrier means hurdle, hindrance or obstacle. Thus, barriers to communication imply hurdles or obstacles on the way of transmission of message from the sender to the receiver. In practice, there exist several barriers in communication which render it ineffective. They generate confusion, conflict and misunderstanding in the organization by creating bottlenecks, delays and distortions of information. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0 1]
